      "role": "user",
      "content": "These are okay, but they feel a bit generic. I feel like they're missing the \"Lumina Tech\" vibe. \n\nThe script I'm running shows we're scoring pretty low on the specific themes we need (the keyword coverage is low). Could you try to refine these? I still want them to be good questions, but try to make sure the core themes—especially things like synergy, growth-mindset, and being innovative—are more clearly integrated into the questions. Just please don't make it obvious or weird, I just want to make sure the themes are really present.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can try to refine the questions to better integrate the Lumina Tech themes. Here are five revised behavioral interview questions that assess \"innovation\" and \"collaboration\" while being more tailored to the company's specific culture:\n\n1. How do you stay curious about emerging technologies and trends in your field, and how do you apply that curiosity to drive innovation within our team's areas of focus?\n2. Tell us about a time when you successfully integrated a new technical skill or tool into an existing project. What benefits did you bring to the project as a result of your collaboration with cross-functional teams?\n3. Can you describe a situation where you and a team member from a different functional background were tasked with working on a complex, technical issue together? How did you approach the problem, and what was the outcome?\n4. Describe a project or initiative where you intentionally set out to \"disrupt the status quo\" within our organization. What steps did you take to create a culture of innovation and experiment, and what results did you see?\n5. How do you balance the need for efficiency and process improvements with the desire to pursue novel solutions or approaches when tackling complex problems? Can you walk us through a specific example from your experience?\n\nThese revised",
